hey I'm Kurt and I play the resident  before remake  I only played it for 30 minutes I can  say one thing is for sure that this  could be the resident 4 remake fans want  but not the one they're expecting to get  and this can all be illustrated by a  single choice that Capcom made with a  dog and if you know the dog you know the  dog you know what dog  the demo kicks off in the opening  moments where Leon S Kennedy is hot on  the trail to investigate The  Disappearance of the president's  daughter and while it all feels familiar  to the events of the original do not be  fooled because this Resident Evil 4 is a  lot more menacing than returning players  might expect this time around Leon is  trudging through a moonlit forest and  the sense of impending dread is on Full  display the sound of buzzing flies the  squawks of crows and the rotting mound  of animal carcasses stacked along the  path emphasizes the more horror-centric  tone  now I don't want to reveal too many  details about the opening Shack scene  because I want returning fans to be  surprised but I will say that it  unravels a little differently and it's  absolutely terrifying it subverted my  expectations of the iconic first ganondo  and though subtle the change was enough  for me to start questioning what would  happen around every corner  I was forced to navigate its many  hallways and rooms which felt more  maze-like and to my surprise featured  locked doors that required keys to open  it's a small detail but one that further  sets it apart from the original making  it more akin to traditional Resident  Evil design which the original resin 4  strayed away from the shack felt grimy  disgusting and dilapidated and this all  came to a head with a harrowing first  run-in with the Resident Evil 4 remix  take on the ganondo  with only one ammo clip at my disposal  cornered and trapped I alternated firing  off rounds and desperately fending it  off using my knife which unlike the  original has a durability bar gennados  were revolutionary in the original for  their distinct movements like ducking  out of the way of your Crosshair or  holding their hands in front of their  face to block shots we've come a long  way since then but it's safe to say that  the frenetic characteristics have been  turned up a notch to ensure they're  still a threat  up close their faces are contorted and  grimacing and being grabbed by one  offers a chance to get a little intimate  with the details  like before aiming for the knees will  prompt enemies to fall to the ground  cueing up a prompt to kick their face in  for a knockback effect on the  surrounding villagers and as expected it  felt incredibly cool because Leon is in  fact a very cool dude something new to  the mix were executions sometimes after  Downing a gonado there was an invitation  to press R2 making Leon plunge his knife  into the target sprinting through the  woods I can hear groans and murmurs from  villagers in the distance really giving  the sensation of being surrounded on all  sides and if my anxiety wasn't high  enough that's when I came across the dog  in this Resident Evil 4 there is no dog  to save from a bear trap and instead a  murder of crows surrounded its corpse  leg still trapped the message was clear  this Resident Evil 4 is darker and even  more dire than the one you know  through all its subtle changes one thing  remained near identical The Village  scene this was to me a shining moment  that Capcom knows not to fix because it  certainly ain't Brook instead the  remarkable difference is the  introduction of stealth this time Leon  can Crouch and move around creating the  opportunity to silently pick off enemies  and gather resources but don't be fooled  the Rampage of villagers hunting you  down is still inevitable the moment  you're spotted is a white knuckled  Sprint to stay alive as you are  surrounded on all sides I scrambled  through doors jumped through Windows  avoided dozens of gonados that lurched  at me or threw hatchets from all angles  I'd pop one of the knees kicking into  the crowd only to be grabbed from behind  triggering a Parry attack to plunge my  knife into their face while ammo was  scarce materials to make weren't either  scavenged through drawers to find  supplies to craft ammunition and health  items another design Trope carried over  from the broader series and through the  chaos and frantic control troller  crunching Leon still managed to toss out  one-liners at a much needed levity with  a casual feel me for the repairs later  Leon you just set an innocent cow on  fire dude how are you this cool the  chaos I was so familiar with from the  original was turn up to 11 this time  around the way the gennados now move  bump into each other and scramble to  tear you apart with their bare hands is  only topped in intensity by the menacing  presence of the Chainsaw man  who now smashes through the environment  to get to you  adding an extra maniacal presence to an  already high stress situation when the  demo ended I could still feel my heart  pounding through my chest  a major takeaway was the emphasis on  Survival horror specifically now this is  interesting because the original made  such a distinction away from its  survival horror Roots only for the  Remake to reaffirm it now it seems like  Capcom is making a very deliberate  effort to try and balance action and  survival I'm of course I'm eager to see  if they can really pull it off Resident  Evil 4 remake doesn't feel like it's  aiming to revolutionize games the way  the original did 17 years ago instead  Capcom is doubling down on what has made  Verizon before Timeless all these years  later its design its tension and of  course Leon S Kennedy in doing so its  goal is to emphasize what remains great  while fine-tuning it with everything the  franchise has learned in its 26 years of  existence  so far it feels like Capcom knows what  it needs to add an order for this game  to stand on its own especially among a  new generation of horror games not to  mention a plethora of remakes that we  have coming out of the way including  Dead Space alone in the dark and now  Silent Hill 2. but from what I can tell  Capcom knows what it needs to add in  order to please returning Fanatics like  me and yes the Bingo line  it's there
 

